    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e64d7d10_7dd5bdb3",
        "filename": "board/flapjack/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 137,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-18T01:22:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note to myself: \nThe thing is cbi_board_override is part of APIs which can be called in any order any time. \n\nIf cbi_get_sku_id is called first, we have to make a decision whether to get panel id from ADC or not before we know board_version. One option is to return EC_SUCCESS and leave SKU_ID alone. However, it can create a discrepancy between the first call and the 2nd call.\n\nSo, we should explicitly return EC_ERROR_BUSY. That\u0027ll make the APIs return consistent results. Once you return EC_SUCCESS, we have to keep returning the same data.\n\nUpdated the function description.",
      "parentUuid": "58716d75_025be1c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 137,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "f791bd8b60a32ed30a5c6be19f3f5776e95b1b07",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
